  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A disc is rolling without slipping on a surface. The radius of the disc is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></math> At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the top most point on the disc is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> as shown in figure. When the disc completes half of its rotation, the displacement of point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> from its initial position is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1661e2e0-9615-435b-a5cf-d959ee5a0044.png\" style=\"width: 380px; height: 210px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
